From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] hvf: a free page report gives the old pages back to macOS

Applies after qemu-hvf-free-page-reclaim.patch and
qemu-hvf-mapped-sections.patch (both left as they are).

What: hvf_report_free_pages() moves the reported range's old memory aside
(mach_vm_remap: one more mapping of the same pages, none touched) before the
fresh MAP_FIXED mapping takes its place (omacvm_reclaim_backing()). A
worker thread ("omacvm-reclaim", utility QoS) then advises the old range
MADV_FREE_REUSABLE and unmaps it (omacvm_reclaim_release()): macOS drops
its compressed copies at once and takes its resident pages first, without
compressing them. Pages macOS is compressing at that very moment are
skipped; the worker looks again 20 ms later and advises once more (twice at
most). Nothing is advised under the main lock: a range that cannot go to
the worker (its queue of 4096 ranges is full, or there is no room to move
it aside) gets the new backing alone, as up to 3.2.11, and qemu.log counts
it. OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0: the new backing alone, as up to 3.2.11.
If macOS keeps the pages anyway, the move aside stops for the run (the
replacement alone): on a refused madvise, or when the releases of 64 MB the
Mac held leave half or more of it held (XNU skips the advice without an
error on memory it does not take as copy-delay; the worker measures what
each release leaves). One qemu.log line says why, and the file
OMACVM_RECLAIM_STATUS names gets "reclaim=keeps" and the reason: the app
then turns off its give-back while macOS compresses the VM for the run.
The worker's first qemu.log line carries the text the app looks for in
QEMU's binary to turn that give-back on (MemoryGiveBack.reclaimMarker;
prepare-qemu-gpu-runtime.sh checks a runtime has it).
qemu.log gets a line an hour while the guest reports, and one at exit:
reports, MB reported, blocks, how long each report held the main lock in
hvf_report_free_pages() (all of it; p99, longest), MB not moved aside and
why, and what the worker released and how much of that is still on the Mac
(resident and not reusable, or compressed: macOS takes reusable pages
first, so they count as given back).
OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK=1 (tests only): a line per report with what its range
held before the release and what it left after.

Why: MAP_FIXED alone only drops QEMU's mapping. XNU frees the pages of an
anonymous object when the whole object goes, and guest RAM is a few
128 MB objects that stay mapped around a reported range: the old pages
stayed resident or compressed, counted in no footprint, until QEMU quit.
A host test kept 1.0 of 1.0 GB "freed" until exit; a 4 GB VM after a
browser session still held 1.6 of the 3.3 GB it had reported, 88 % of it
compressed. Activity Monitor's figure for the VM falls either way; this is
memory it never showed. XNU applies the advice to a shared object only
when it is copy-delay (vm_map_reusable_pages); hv_vm_map makes guest RAM
exactly that (true share, ref >= 2), which the test checks first. The
advice costs about 0.1 ms per MB the Mac still holds (MacBook Air M2): up
to 21.5 ms per report when it ran under the main lock (MAP_FIXED alone:
1.3-3.2 ms), and the guest stood still for 107-160 ms, so it runs on the
worker.

Upstream: OmacVM only (upstream QEMU discards a report with
madvise(MADV_DONTNEED), which keeps guest-dirtied pages on macOS).
Test: Tests/memory/test-reclaim.sh, no VM: guest RAM shared with a second
map or a real hv_vm_map, split by earlier reports; after each report and
its release the old pages are neither resident (unless reusable) nor
compressed, but for those macOS was compressing at that very moment (up to
5 % allowed), and the pages around keep their data. main's helper and
OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0 fail it (Mac mini, macOS 27, real hv_vm_map,
region compressed first: main left 4832 of 4848 pages compressed, the
advice 0). Its --keeps part: a refused madvise (a read-only range) and an
advice XNU skips (memory a child process shares) stop the move aside and
write the status file; releases that work do neither. Its --overflow part:
with the worker held back until its queue is full, one more report, and
then a range with no room to move aside, get the new backing alone, with
no advice under the BQL, and are counted; each report's hold covers all it
did under the BQL; the worker then releases what it was given; the run's
qemu.log line says "reported", what was not moved aside and why, and its
p99 is never above the longest hold. The runtime build runs it on the
patched source, CI on this file.

--- a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
+++ b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
@@ -17,13 +17,18 @@
 #include "system/address-spaces.h"
 #include "system/memory.h"
 #include "system/ramblock.h"
+#include "system/system.h"
 #include "qemu/main-loop.h"
+#include "qemu/timer.h"
 #include "system/hvf.h"
 #include "system/hvf_int.h"
 #include "hw/core/cpu.h"
 #include "hw/core/boards.h"
 #include "trace.h"
 
+#include <mach/mach.h>
+#include <mach/mach_vm.h>
+
 bool hvf_allowed;
 bool hvf_kernel_irqchip;
 bool hvf_nested_virt;
@@ -160,6 +165,563 @@ static void hvf_set_phys_mem(MemoryRegionSection *section, bool add)
     g_hash_table_add(hvf_mapped_sections, g_memdup2(&gpa, sizeof(gpa)));
 }
 
+/* omacvm-reclaim: begin (app/runtime/Tests/memory/test-reclaim.sh builds this part alone) */
+/*
+ * Give the pages of a reported free range back to macOS.
+ *
+ * Darwin's MADV_DONTNEED keeps guest-dirtied RAM, so the range gets a fresh
+ * demand-zero mapping at the same address (MAP_FIXED: no unreserved gap).
+ * That alone only drops QEMU's mapping: macOS frees the pages of an
+ * anonymous object when the whole object goes, and guest RAM is a few large
+ * objects (128 MB each) that stay mapped around the range. The old pages
+ * stayed resident or compressed, counted in no footprint, until QEMU quit.
+ *
+ * So the old range first moves aside (one more mapping of the same memory,
+ * mach_vm_remap: no page is touched), and a worker thread advises it
+ * MADV_FREE_REUSABLE and unmaps it (omacvm_reclaim_release()): macOS drops
+ * the compressed copies at once and takes the resident pages first, without
+ * compressing them. XNU does that for guest RAM, which the hypervisor's map
+ * shares (copy-delay, ref >= 2; Tests/memory/test-reclaim.c with a real
+ * hv_vm_map). The advice costs about 0.1 ms per MB the Mac still held (M2):
+ * under the BQL it held the lock up to 21.5 ms for one report and stalled
+ * the guest, so nothing advises under the BQL. Pages macOS is compressing
+ * at that moment are skipped by the advice; the worker looks again 20 ms
+ * later and advises once more (twice at most). The guest touches none of
+ * these pages until QEMU acknowledges the report, and the fresh mapping
+ * takes the range before that, so the reusable state stays on pages that no
+ * guest mapping reaches again. Order: the stage-2 unmap (no vCPU reaches the
+ * range), the move aside, the new backing, the stage-2 map.
+ *
+ * A range that cannot go to the worker (its queue is full, or there is no
+ * room to move the range aside) gets the new backing alone, as up to
+ * 3.2.11: what the Mac held of it stays until QEMU quits. qemu.log counts
+ * it. So does OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0 (the new backing alone throughout).
+ *
+ * If macOS keeps the pages anyway (a refused madvise, or an advice it skips
+ * without an error: memory it does not take as copy-delay), the move aside
+ * stops for the run (omacvm_reclaim_keeps()): one qemu.log line, and the
+ * file OMACVM_RECLAIM_STATUS names says "reclaim=keeps", so the app turns
+ * off its give-back while macOS compresses the VM (ADR 0062).
+ */
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimPages {
+    uint64_t resident, compressed;       /* bytes the Mac still holds */
+} OmacvmReclaimPages;
+
+/* 1: move aside and advise; 0: the new backing alone (switched off, or macOS keeps the pages) */
+static int omacvm_reclaim_reusable = -1;
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_kept;
+
+/* Under the BQL. The worker may set it to 0 (omacvm_reclaim_keeps()). */
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_on(void)
+{
+    int on = __atomic_load_n(&omacvm_reclaim_reusable, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+
+    if (on < 0) {
+        const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE");
+        on = !(v && !strcmp(v, "0"));
+        __atomic_store_n(&omacvm_reclaim_reusable, on, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
+/*
+ * macOS keeps the pages the guest gives back: no more moves aside this run,
+ * once. The app reads OMACVM_RECLAIM_STATUS's file every 5 s.
+ */
+static void omacvm_reclaim_keeps(const char *why)
+{
+    const char *path = getenv("OMACVM_RECLAIM_STATUS");
+    char text[256];
+    int fd, n;
+
+    if (__atomic_exchange_n(&omacvm_reclaim_kept, true, __ATOMIC_RELAXED)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    __atomic_store_n(&omacvm_reclaim_reusable, 0, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+    warn_report("OmacVM: free page reclaim: macOS keeps the pages the VM "
+                "gives back (%s): the new backing alone from now on, as up "
+                "to 3.2.11", why);
+    if (!path || !*path) {
+        return;
+    }
+    n = snprintf(text, sizeof(text), "reclaim=keeps\nwhy=%s\n", why);
+    fd = open(path, O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | O_CLOEXEC, 0644);
+    if (fd < 0) {
+        return;                             /* qemu.log has it */
+    }
+    if (write(fd, text, n < (int)sizeof(text) ? n : (int)sizeof(text) - 1) < 0) {
+        /* qemu.log has it */
+    }
+    close(fd);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_refusal(int err)
+{
+    char why[96];
+
+    snprintf(why, sizeof(why), "madvise refused: %s", strerror(err));
+    omacvm_reclaim_keeps(why);
+}
+
+/*
+ * An advice macOS skips returns no error, so the worker also looks: once the
+ * releases of a window found 64 MB the Mac held, half or more of it still
+ * held after them means macOS keeps the pages (the advice leaves none but
+ * pages it was compressing at that moment: 0-2 % in the tests; no advice:
+ * all of them). false then, with the reason in why.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_WINDOW (64ull << 20)
+
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimJudge {
+    uint64_t held, left;                 /* bytes, this window */
+} OmacvmReclaimJudge;
+
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_takes(OmacvmReclaimJudge *j, OmacvmReclaimPages before,
+                                 OmacvmReclaimPages left, char *why, size_t len)
+{
+    bool ok;
+
+    j->held += before.resident + before.compressed;
+    j->left += left.resident + left.compressed;
+    if (j->held < OMACVM_RECLAIM_WINDOW) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    ok = j->left * 2 < j->held;
+    if (!ok) {
+        snprintf(why, len, "%" PRIu64 " of %" PRIu64 " MB the Mac held stayed "
+                 "after the advice", j->left >> 20, j->held >> 20);
+    }
+    j->held = j->left = 0;
+    return ok;
+}
+
+/* What the Mac still holds of [at, at + size): resident and not reusable, or compressed. */
+static OmacvmReclaimPages omacvm_reclaim_held(mach_vm_address_t at, size_t size)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimPages held = { 0, 0 };
+    size_t page = (size_t)getpagesize();
+    int disp[256];
+    mach_vm_size_t off = 0, n, i;
+
+    while (off < size) {
+        n = (size - off) / page < 256 ? (size - off) / page : 256;
+        if (mach_vm_page_range_query(mach_task_self(), at + off, n * page,
+                                     (mach_vm_address_t)disp, &n) != KERN_SUCCESS || !n) {
+            break;
+        }
+        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+            if (disp[i] & VM_PAGE_QUERY_PAGE_PAGED_OUT) {
+                held.compressed += page;
+            } else if ((disp[i] & VM_PAGE_QUERY_PAGE_PRESENT) &&
+                       !(disp[i] & VM_PAGE_QUERY_PAGE_REUSABLE)) {
+                held.resident += page;
+            }
+        }
+        off += n * page;
+    }
+    return held;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Under the BQL: the new backing for a reported range. aside: move the old
+ * range aside first, for omacvm_reclaim_release() on the worker. Returns
+ * where it went (0: not moved; what the Mac held of it stays, as up to
+ * 3.2.11). Never advises: that costs too long under the BQL.
+ */
+static mach_vm_address_t omacvm_reclaim_backing(hwaddr gpa, void *host,
+                                                size_t size,
+                                                hv_memory_flags_t flags,
+                                                bool aside)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t at = 0;
+    vm_prot_t cur, max;
+    void *replacement;
+
+    trace_hvf_vm_unmap(gpa, size);
+    assert_hvf_ok(hv_vm_unmap(gpa, size));
+    if (aside &&
+        mach_vm_remap(mach_task_self(), &at, size, 0, VM_FLAGS_ANYWHERE,
+                      mach_task_self(), (mach_vm_address_t)host, FALSE,
+                      &cur, &max, VM_INHERIT_NONE) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        at = 0;                             /* no room: the new backing alone */
+    }
+    replacement = mmap(host, size, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE,
+                       MAP_FIXED | MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANON, -1, 0);
+    if (replacement == MAP_FAILED) {
+        error_report("HVF free-page backing replacement failed: %s",
+                     strerror(errno));
+        abort();
+    }
+    assert(replacement == host);
+    trace_hvf_vm_map(gpa, size, host, flags,
+                     flags & HV_MEMORY_READ ? 'R' : '-',
+                     flags & HV_MEMORY_WRITE ? 'W' : '-',
+                     flags & HV_MEMORY_EXEC ? 'X' : '-');
+    assert_hvf_ok(hv_vm_map(host, gpa, size, flags));
+    return at;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The worker, for a range moved aside: advise it and unmap it. Pages still
+ * held 20 ms later are advised once more, twice at most. Returns what is
+ * still on the Mac after all; *before (when not NULL): what it held first.
+ */
+static OmacvmReclaimPages omacvm_reclaim_release(mach_vm_address_t aside,
+                                                 size_t size,
+                                                 OmacvmReclaimPages *before)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimPages left = { 0, 0 };
+    bool refused;
+    int tries;
+
+    if (before) {
+        *before = omacvm_reclaim_held(aside, size);
+    }
+    for (tries = 0; tries < 3; tries++) {
+        if (tries) {
+            usleep(20000);
+        }
+        refused = madvise((void *)aside, size, MADV_FREE_REUSABLE) != 0;
+        if (refused) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_refusal(errno);
+        }
+        left = omacvm_reclaim_held(aside, size);
+        if (refused || (!left.resident && !left.compressed)) {
+            break;                          /* no point in asking again */
+        }
+    }
+    munmap((void *)aside, size);
+    return left;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The worker: releases the ranges moved aside, in order, at utility QoS.
+ * Only the BQL's holder adds to the queue, and it looks for room before it
+ * moves a range aside (omacvm_reclaim_room()): the room stays until it adds.
+ * A marker item (aside 0) closes a report for OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK's line.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE 4096
+
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimItem {
+    mach_vm_address_t aside;
+    size_t size;
+    int64_t hold_ns;                    /* a marker: the report's hold */
+} OmacvmReclaimItem;
+
+static struct {
+    QemuMutex lock;
+    QemuCond more;
+    QemuThread thread;
+    bool started;
+    unsigned head, count;
+    OmacvmReclaimItem item[OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE];
+    /* under lock: what the releases left (OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK: and held) */
+    uint64_t released, left_resident, left_compressed;
+    uint64_t held_before, compressed_before;
+} omacvm_reclaim_w;
+
+/*
+ * What free page reporting gave back, for qemu.log: a line an hour while the
+ * guest reports, and one at exit. A report is one virtqueue element (Linux
+ * sends up to 32 blocks and waits for each); its hold is the time its blocks
+ * kept the BQL in hvf_report_free_pages(), all of it: the checks, unmap,
+ * move aside, new backing, map and queueing. Under the BQL.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS 100000     /* hold histogram: 0.1 ms steps */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS 400          /* the last one counts 40 ms and up */
+
+/* Why ranges were not moved aside (their old pages stay on the Mac). */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_OFF    1u      /* OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0 */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_KEPT   2u      /* macOS keeps the pages: stopped */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_FULL   4u      /* the worker's queue was full */
+#define OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_NOROOM 8u      /* no room to move the range aside */
+
+static const char *const omacvm_reclaim_whys[] = {
+    "OMACVM_RECLAIM_REUSABLE=0", "macOS keeps the pages",
+    "the worker's queue was full", "no room to move them aside",
+};
+
+typedef struct OmacvmReclaimStats {
+    uint64_t reports, blocks, bytes, in_place;
+    unsigned why;
+    int64_t longest_ns;
+    uint32_t hold[OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS];
+} OmacvmReclaimStats;
+
+static struct {
+    uint64_t blocks, bytes, in_place, queued;
+    unsigned why;
+    int64_t ns;
+} omacvm_reclaim_cur;
+static OmacvmReclaimStats omacvm_reclaim_hour, omacvm_reclaim_run;
+static int64_t omacvm_reclaim_hour_start;
+static int omacvm_reclaim_check = -1;
+static Notifier omacvm_reclaim_exit;
+
+/* OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK=1 (tests only): a line per report with what it left on the Mac. */
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_check_on(void)
+{
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_check < 0) {
+        const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_RECLAIM_CHECK");
+        omacvm_reclaim_check = v && !strcmp(v, "1");
+    }
+    return omacvm_reclaim_check;
+}
+
+static double omacvm_reclaim_mb(uint64_t bytes)
+{
+    return bytes / (1024.0 * 1024.0);
+}
+
+static void *omacvm_reclaim_work(void *opaque)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimItem it;
+    OmacvmReclaimPages before = { 0, 0 }, left, rb = { 0, 0 }, rl = { 0, 0 };
+    OmacvmReclaimJudge judge = { 0, 0 };
+    uint64_t blocks = 0, bytes = 0;
+    bool check = omacvm_reclaim_check_on();
+    char why[128];
+
+    pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_UTILITY, 0);
+    /* The app looks for this text in QEMU's binary (MemoryGiveBack.reclaimMarker). */
+    info_report("OmacVM: free page reclaim gives the pages back to macOS "
+                "(MADV_FREE_REUSABLE on its own thread)");
+    for (;;) {
+        qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        while (!omacvm_reclaim_w.count) {
+            qemu_cond_wait(&omacvm_reclaim_w.more, &omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        }
+        it = omacvm_reclaim_w.item[omacvm_reclaim_w.head];
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.head = (omacvm_reclaim_w.head + 1) % OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE;
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.count--;
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        if (!it.aside) {
+            if (check && blocks) {
+                info_report("OmacVM: reclaim check: %" PRIu64 " blocks, %.1f MB: "
+                            "%.1f MB held before (%.1f MB compressed), %.1f MB "
+                            "left resident, %.1f MB left compressed; hold %.2f ms",
+                            blocks, omacvm_reclaim_mb(bytes),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rb.resident + rb.compressed),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rb.compressed),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rl.resident),
+                            omacvm_reclaim_mb(rl.compressed), it.hold_ns / 1e6);
+            }
+            blocks = bytes = 0;
+            rb = rl = (OmacvmReclaimPages) { 0, 0 };
+            continue;
+        }
+        left = omacvm_reclaim_release(it.aside, it.size, &before);
+        if (!omacvm_reclaim_takes(&judge, before, left, why, sizeof(why))) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_keeps(why);
+        }
+        qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.released += it.size;
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.left_resident += left.resident;
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.left_compressed += left.compressed;
+        if (check) {
+            omacvm_reclaim_w.held_before += before.resident + before.compressed;
+            omacvm_reclaim_w.compressed_before += before.compressed;
+        }
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        if (check) {
+            blocks++;
+            bytes += it.size;
+            rb.resident += before.resident;
+            rb.compressed += before.compressed;
+            rl.resident += left.resident;
+            rl.compressed += left.compressed;
+        }
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+/* Under the BQL: is there room on the worker's queue for one more range? */
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_room(void)
+{
+    bool room;
+
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_w.started) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    room = omacvm_reclaim_w.count < OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE;
+    qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    return room;
+}
+
+/* Under the BQL: a range (or a marker) to the worker. false: no room. */
+static bool omacvm_reclaim_queue(mach_vm_address_t aside, size_t size,
+                                 int64_t hold_ns)
+{
+    OmacvmReclaimItem *it;
+
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_w.started) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_w.started = true;
+        qemu_mutex_init(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        qemu_cond_init(&omacvm_reclaim_w.more);
+        qemu_thread_create(&omacvm_reclaim_w.thread, "omacvm-reclaim",
+                           omacvm_reclaim_work, NULL, QEMU_THREAD_DETACHED);
+    }
+    qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_w.count == OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE) {
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        return false;
+    }
+    it = &omacvm_reclaim_w.item[(omacvm_reclaim_w.head + omacvm_reclaim_w.count) %
+                                OMACVM_RECLAIM_QUEUE];
+    it->aside = aside;
+    it->size = size;
+    it->hold_ns = hold_ns;
+    omacvm_reclaim_w.count++;
+    qemu_cond_signal(&omacvm_reclaim_w.more);
+    qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Under the BQL, one block of a report that hvf_report_free_pages() checked
+ * since start: the new backing, and the old range to the worker. All of it
+ * counts in the report's hold.
+ */
+static void omacvm_reclaim_report(int64_t start, hwaddr gpa, void *host,
+                                  size_t size, hv_memory_flags_t flags)
+{
+    unsigned why = 0;
+    mach_vm_address_t aside;
+
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_on()) {
+        why = __atomic_load_n(&omacvm_reclaim_kept, __ATOMIC_RELAXED) ?
+              OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_KEPT : OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_OFF;
+    } else if (!omacvm_reclaim_room()) {
+        why = OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_FULL;
+    }
+    aside = omacvm_reclaim_backing(gpa, host, size, flags, !why);
+    if (!why && !aside) {
+        why = OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_NOROOM;
+    } else if (aside && !omacvm_reclaim_queue(aside, size, 0)) {
+        munmap((void *)aside, size);        /* room was checked: not expected */
+        aside = 0;
+        why = OMACVM_RECLAIM_WHY_FULL;
+    }
+    if (aside) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_cur.queued++;
+    } else {
+        omacvm_reclaim_cur.in_place += size;
+        omacvm_reclaim_cur.why |= why;
+    }
+    omacvm_reclaim_cur.blocks++;
+    omacvm_reclaim_cur.bytes += size;
+    omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns += get_clock() - start;
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_log(const char *when, const OmacvmReclaimStats *s)
+{
+    uint64_t need = s->reports - s->reports / 100, seen = 0;
+    g_autofree char *not_aside = NULL;
+    g_autofree char *worker = NULL;
+    char why[160] = "";
+    int64_t p99;
+    size_t n;
+    int step, i;
+
+    if (!s->reports) {
+        return;
+    }
+    for (step = 0; step < OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1; step++) {
+        seen += s->hold[step];
+        if (seen >= need) {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    /* The step's upper end, never above the longest hold. */
+    p99 = MIN((int64_t)(step + 1) * OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS, s->longest_ns);
+    if (s->in_place) {
+        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+            n = strlen(why);
+            if (s->why & (1u << i)) {
+                snprintf(why + n, sizeof(why) - n, "%s%s", n ? ", " : "",
+                         omacvm_reclaim_whys[i]);
+            }
+        }
+        not_aside = g_strdup_printf("; %.1f MB not moved aside (%s): what the "
+                                    "Mac held of it stays until QEMU quits",
+                                    omacvm_reclaim_mb(s->in_place), why);
+    }
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_w.started) {
+        qemu_mutex_lock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+        worker = g_strdup_printf("; this run the worker released %.0f MB, %.1f MB "
+                                 "of it left on the Mac (%.1f resident, %.1f "
+                                 "compressed)",
+                                 omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.released),
+                                 omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.left_resident +
+                                                   omacvm_reclaim_w.left_compressed),
+                                 omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.left_resident),
+                                 omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.left_compressed));
+        if (omacvm_reclaim_check_on()) {
+            char *c = g_strdup_printf("%s; check: %.0f MB held before (%.0f MB "
+                                      "compressed)", worker,
+                                      omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.held_before),
+                                      omacvm_reclaim_mb(omacvm_reclaim_w.compressed_before));
+            g_free(worker);
+            worker = c;
+        }
+        qemu_mutex_unlock(&omacvm_reclaim_w.lock);
+    }
+    info_report("OmacVM: free page reporting %s: %" PRIu64 " reports, %.0f MB "
+                "reported in %" PRIu64 " blocks; main lock held per report p99 "
+                "%.2f ms, longest %.2f ms%s%s", when, s->reports,
+                omacvm_reclaim_mb(s->bytes), s->blocks, p99 / 1e6,
+                s->longest_ns / 1e6, not_aside ? not_aside : "", worker ? worker : "");
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_at_exit(Notifier *n, void *data)
+{
+    omacvm_reclaim_log("this run", &omacvm_reclaim_run);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_reclaim_add(OmacvmReclaimStats *s, int step)
+{
+    s->reports++;
+    s->blocks += omacvm_reclaim_cur.blocks;
+    s->bytes += omacvm_reclaim_cur.bytes;
+    s->in_place += omacvm_reclaim_cur.in_place;
+    s->why |= omacvm_reclaim_cur.why;
+    s->longest_ns = MAX(s->longest_ns, omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns);
+    s->hold[step]++;
+}
+
+void hvf_report_free_pages_done(void)
+{
+    int64_t now = get_clock();
+    int step;
+
+    assert(bql_locked());
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_cur.blocks) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (!omacvm_reclaim_hour_start) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_hour_start = now;
+        omacvm_reclaim_exit.notify = omacvm_reclaim_at_exit;
+        qemu_add_exit_notifier(&omacvm_reclaim_exit);
+    }
+    if (omacvm_reclaim_check_on() && omacvm_reclaim_cur.queued) {
+        /* No room for the marker: that report's check line joins the next. */
+        omacvm_reclaim_queue(0, 0, omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns);
+        omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns += get_clock() - now;
+    }
+    step = MIN(omacvm_reclaim_cur.ns / OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS,
+               OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1);
+    omacvm_reclaim_add(&omacvm_reclaim_hour, step);
+    omacvm_reclaim_add(&omacvm_reclaim_run, step);
+    memset(&omacvm_reclaim_cur, 0, sizeof(omacvm_reclaim_cur));
+    if (now - omacvm_reclaim_hour_start >= 3600 * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND) {
+        omacvm_reclaim_log("in the last hour", &omacvm_reclaim_hour);
+        memset(&omacvm_reclaim_hour, 0, sizeof(omacvm_reclaim_hour));
+        omacvm_reclaim_hour_start = now;
+    }
+}
+/* omacvm-reclaim: end */
